          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em one-point compactification
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a new
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^* = X \cup \{\infty\}
            obtained by adding a single new point “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            ” to the original space and declaring in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^*
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
            of the original
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspaces"} subspaces
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspace"} open
          %p
            One may think of the adjoined point as the “point at infinity” of the original space. A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishes at infinity
            precisely if it extends to a continuous function on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^*
            and literally takes the value zero at the point “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            ”.
          %p
            This one-point compactification is also known as the
            %em Alexandroff compactification
            after a 1924 paper by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Aleksandrov"} Павел Сергеевич Александров
            (then transliterated ‘P.S. Aleksandroff’).
          %p
            The one-point compactification is usually applied to a non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
            space. In the more general situation, it may not really be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactification"} compactification
            and hence is called the
            %em one-point extension
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em Alexandroff extension
          %p
            Applied to a non-compact space, the one-point compactification is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end+compactification"} end compactification
            (where each “end”, hence each “connected component of infinity” appears as a separate point) by the set of ends.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#for_topological_spaces For topological spaces
          #OnePointExtension.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (one-point extension)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %strong one-point extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^*
              is the topological space
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  whose underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \cup \{\infty\}
                  of that of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton set
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\infty\}
              %li
                %p
                  and whose
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
                  are
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
                      of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \,\subset\, X^*
                      ;
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mo *
                            %mo ∖
                            %mi CK
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ∖
                            %mi CK
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast \setminus CK = (X \setminus CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                      of the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
                      subsets
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi CK
                              %mo ⊂
                              %mi X
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \subset X
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Aleksandrov24"}> Aleksandrov 24
            , see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Kelley75"} Kelley 75, p. 150
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspaces+of+Hausdorff+spaces+are+closed"} compact subspaces of Hausdorff spaces are closed
          #OnePointExtensionWellDefined.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong (one-point extension is well-defined)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
              on the one-point extension in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              is indeed well defined in that the given set of subsets is indeed closed under arbitrary unions and finite intersections.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The unions and finite intersections of the open subsets inherited from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are closed among themselves by the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a topological space.
            %p It is hence sufficient to see that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the unions and finite intersection of the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo \
                        %mi CK
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                  are closed among themselves,
              %li
                %p
                  the union and intersection of a subset of the form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %munder
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mtext open
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \underset{\text{open}}{\subset} X \subset X^\ast
                  with one of the form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo \
                        %mi CK
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                  is again of one of the two kinds.
            %p
              Regarding the first statement: Under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"} de Morgan duality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %munder
                          %mi J
                          %mtext finite
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi CK
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %munder
                              %mi J
                              %mtext finite
                        %msub
                          %mi CK
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in \underset{\text{finite}}{J}}{\bigcap} (X \backslash CK_i \cup \{\infty\})
                    \=
                    \\left( X \backslash \left(\underset{i \in \underset{\text{finite}}{J}}{\bigcup} CK_i \right)\right) \cup \{\infty\}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi CK
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi CK
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in I}{\bigcup} ( X \backslash CK_i \cup \{\infty\} )
                    \=
                    \\left(X \backslash \left(\underset{i \in I}{\bigcap} CK_i \right)\right) \cup \{\infty\}
            %p
              and so the first statement follows from the fact that finite unions of compact subspaces and arbitrary intersections of closed compact subspaces are themselves again compact (
              %a{:href => "compact+space#UnionsAndIntersectionOfCompactSubspaces"}> this prop.
              ).
            %p
              Regarding the second statement: That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              is open means that there exists a closed subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset X
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = X\backslash C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"} de Morgan duality
              we find
            %ol
              %li
                %p for intersections:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi U
                                %mo ∩
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∩
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi C
                                %mo ∪
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{aligned}
                        U \cap ( (X\backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\} )
                        \&amp; =
                        (X \backslash C) \cap (X \backslash CK)
                        \\\
                        \&amp; =
                        X \backslash (C \cup CK).
                        \\end{aligned}
                %p
                  Since finite unions of closed subsets are closed, this is again an open subset of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p for unions:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi U
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi C
                                %mo ∩
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{aligned}
                        U \cup (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                        \&amp; =
                        (X \backslash C) \cup (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                        \\\
                        \&amp; =
                        (X \backslash (C \cap CK)) \cup \{\infty\} .
                        \\end{aligned}
                %p
                  For this to be open in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
                  we need that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi CK
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \cap CK
                  is again compact. This follows because
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets+are+closed+in+a+closed+subspace+precisely+if+they+are+closed+in+the+ambient+space"} subsets are closed in a closed subspace precisely if they are closed in the ambient space
                  and because
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} closed subsets of compact spaces are compact
          %h3#for_noncommutative_topological_spaces_algebras
            For non-commutative topological spaces (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            \-algebras)
          %p
            Dually in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+topology"} non-commutative topology
            the one-point compactification corresponds to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitisation+of+C%2A-algebras"} unitisation of C*-algebras
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#BasicProperties Basic properties
          %p
            We discuss the basic properties of the construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
            in def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtensionIsCompact"}
            below) and the ingredients needed to see its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            in the Hausdorff case
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#OnePointExtensionIsCompact"} below
          #OnePointExtensionIsCompact.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (one-point extension is compact)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X^\ast\}_{i \in I}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %p That we have a cover means that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  there must exist
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_\infty \in I
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mn ∞
                        %mo ⊃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{i \infty} \supset \{\infty\}
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
                  of the extra point. But since, by construction, the only open subsets containing that point are of the form
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo \
                          %mi CK
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CK
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \subset X
                  with
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo \
                          %mi CK
                          %mo ⊂
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \backslash CK \subset U_{i \infty}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in i}
                  is in particular an open cover of that closed compact subset
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi CK
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \subset X
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset I
                  so that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} J
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \J \subset X}
                  is still a cover of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi CK
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK
            %p Together this implies that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi I
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in J \subset I}
                    \\cup
                    \\{ U_{i_\infty} \}
            %p is a finite subcover of the original cover.
          #HausdorffOnePointCompactification.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (one-point extension of locally compact space is Hausdorff precisely if original space is)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              It is clear that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is not Hausdorff then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              is not.
            %p
              For the converse, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is Hausdorff.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast = X \cup \{\infty\}
              as underlying sets, we only need to check that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              any point, then there is an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \subset X \subset X^\ast
              and an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\infty \subset X^\ast
              of the extra point which are disjoint.
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is locally compact implies by definition that there exists an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_k \supset \{x\}
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CK
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \coloneqq Cl(U_x)
              is a closed compact neighbourhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CK
                      %mo ⊃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \supset \{x\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mi CK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_\infty \coloneqq (X \backslash CK ) \cup \{\infty\} \subset X^\ast
            %p
              is an open neighbourhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\infty\}
              and the two are disjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_x \cap V_\infty = \emptyset
            %p by construction.
          #InclusionIntoOnePointExtensionIsOpenEmbedding.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (inclusion into one-point extension is open embedding)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow X^\ast
            %p
              into its one-point extension (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"} open map
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedding of topological spaces
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Regarding the first point: For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              open and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CK
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \subset X
              closed and compact, the preimages of the corresponding open subsets in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mi CK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mi CK
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i^{-1}(U) = U
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    i^{-1}( (X \backslash CK) \cup \infty ) = X \backslash CK
            %p
              which are open in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Regarding the second point: The image of an open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(U) = U \subset X^\ast
            %p
              Regarding the third point: We need to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon X \to i(X) \subset X^\ast
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
          #CompactHausdorffSpaceIsCompactificationOfComplementOfAnyPoint.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0 \in X
              any point, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to the one-point compactification (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \setminus \{x_0\} \subset X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \simeq (X \setminus \{x_0\})^\ast
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe also that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \setminus \{x_0\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspace"} open subspace
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspaces+of+compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+locally+compact"} open subspaces of compact Hausdorff spaces are locally compact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              Since
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspaces+of+compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+equivalently+compact+subspaces"} closed subspaces of compact Hausdorff spaces are equivalently compact subspaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              are equivalently the complements of closed, and hence compact closed, subsets in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \setminus \{x\}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              this means that the function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ∖
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; (X \setminus \{x_0\})^\ast
                    }
            %p
              which is the identity on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \setminus \{x_0\}
              and sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↦
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0 \mapsto \infty
              (hence which is just the identity on the underlying sets) is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
          %h3#UniversalProperty Universal property
          %p
            As a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            may be described by a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
          %p
            For every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, y_0)
            and every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(K)
            is compact for all closed sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            not containing
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast \to Y
            that extends
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            To see this, note that such a map is necessarily unique. It suffices to show existence. Extend
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast: X^\ast \to Y
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty\mapsto y_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subset Y
            is open, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ∉
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_0\notin U
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^\ast)^{-1}(U) = f^{-1}(U)
            is open. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_0\in U
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∖
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\setminus U
            is closed and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∖
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(Y\setminus U)
            is compact, by the hypothesis. Put
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = f^{-1}(Y\setminus U)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is closed and compact and so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo ∖
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^\ast)^{-1}(U) = X^\ast\setminus K
            is open. It follows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
            is continuous.
          %p
            This property characterizes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+unique"} essentially unique
            manner.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subspace"} dense
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
