            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is already both Hausdorff and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact
            (see prop.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffOnePointCompactification"}
          %h3#MonoidalFunctoriality Functoriality
          %p
          #OnePointCompactificationFunctor.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
            %p
              The operation of one-point compactification (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              on the whole
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} locally compact Hausdorff spaces
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"} proper maps
              between them:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi LCHaus
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ProperMaps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi CHaus
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)^\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (LCHaus, ProperMaps)
                    \\xrightarrow{\;}
                    CHaus^{\ast/}
            %p
              In particular, it is functorial for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core+groupoids"} core groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi LCHaus
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi CHaus
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)^\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Core(LCHaus) \to Core\big(CHaus^{\ast/}\big)
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#James84"} James 1984 bottom of p 70
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Cutler20"} Cutler 20 Prop. 1.6
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/4278178/58526"} MO:a/4278178
          #OnePointCompactificationAndSmashProduct.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification+intertwines+Cartesian+product+with+smash+product"}> one-point compactification intertwines Cartesian product with smash product
                )
            %p
              On the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} locally compact Hausdorff spaces
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"} proper maps
              between them, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\ast
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              (from Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointCompactificationFunctor"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  sends
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+topological+spaces"} disjoint union topological spaces
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sums"} wedge sums
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
              %li
                %p
                  sends
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+spaces"} product topological spaces
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+products"} smash products
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            %p
              hence constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
              for both
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
              structures of these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+monoidal+categories"} distributive monoidal categories
              in that there are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi Y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∨
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    X \sqcup Y
                    \\big)^{\ast}
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    X^{\ast} \vee Y^{\ast}
                    \\,,
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    X \times Y
                    \\big)^{\ast}
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    X^{\ast} \wedge Y^{\ast}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is briefly mentioned in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Bredon93"} Bredon 93, p. 199
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#James84"} James 84 Prop. 3.7 p. 72
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/1645794/58526"} MO:a/1645794
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Cutler20"} Cutler 20, Prop. 1.6
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#general General
          %p
          #OnePointExtensionOfCompactSpace.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is already itself
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with a
