          %h3#compactification_of_discrete_spaces Compactification of discrete spaces
          %p
          #CompactifOfCountableSet.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (one-point compactification of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
              %br/
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              regarded as a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+set"} underlying set
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}
              of the natural numbers with an element “at
              = succeed "\u201D," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity"} infinity
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              are those
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
              that either do not contain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              and are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinite+subsets"} cofinite subsets
            %p
              This space is actually a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+space"} Stone space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+duality"} Stone duality
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
              of the finite and cofinite subsets of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
              operations of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} set-complement
            %p
              To see this, notice that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clopen+sets"} clopen sets
              in the space are those that are either
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              and not containing
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinite+set"} cofinite
              and containing
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              if it is finite. Under this correspondence, the Boolean algebra operations on finite and cofinite subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              correspond to the Boolean algebra operations on the clopen sets.
            %p
              Another reason that this space is important is because to give a continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
